1
00:00:00,430 --> 00:00:04,900
Playing Games

2
00:00:04,900 --> 00:00:06,150
Oh, Daddy!

3
00:00:06,150 --> 00:00:08,100
We had such a good time at the aquarium.

4
00:00:08,100 --> 00:00:09,190
I saw a real shark.

5
00:00:09,190 --> 00:00:10,480
I could almost touch it.

6
00:00:10,480 --> 00:00:12,350
I'm so glad.

7
00:00:12,350 --> 00:00:13,670
Hi. Michelle,

8
00:00:13,670 --> 00:00:15,540
why don't you introduce everybody to Susan?

9
00:00:15,540 --> 00:00:16,150
Hi, Susan.

10
00:00:16,150 --> 00:00:17,420
Hi.

11
00:00:17,420 --> 00:00:20,600
I'd like you to meet Audrey and her mother, Mrs. Cooper.

12
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:21,520
Hello, Audrey.

13
00:00:21,520 --> 00:00:22,840
Nice to meet you, Mrs. Cooper.

14
00:00:22,840 --> 00:00:24,360
I'm Susan Stewart.

15
00:00:24,360 --> 00:00:26,840
And this is Shirley and Nicole.

16
00:00:26,840 --> 00:00:28,480
Hi, girls.

17
00:00:28,480 --> 00:00:28,990
Come on in.

18
00:00:28,990 --> 00:00:29,820
Come on in, Mrs. Cooper.

19
00:00:29,820 --> 00:00:30,750
Come on in, everybody.

20
00:00:30,750 --> 00:00:31,980
The aquarium was so exciting.

21
00:00:31,980 --> 00:00:33,630
I had never been there before.

22
00:00:33,630 --> 00:00:35,470
The girls learned a great deal.

23
00:00:35,470 --> 00:00:35,900
Frankly, so did I.

24
00:00:35,900 --> 00:00:38,270
Well, please sit down

25
00:00:38,270 --> 00:00:40,010
and tell us all about it during lunch.

26
00:00:40,010 --> 00:00:42,000
We prepared some tuna fish

27
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:44,730
and cheese sandwiches for lunch.

28
00:00:44,730 --> 00:00:46,220
I love tuna fish.

29
00:00:46,220 --> 00:00:50,130
Don't you, Audrey?

30
00:00:50,130 --> 00:00:52,500
I remember when I used to be a Girl Scout.

31
00:00:52,500 --> 00:00:55,830
My mother would take us everywhere, too.

32
00:00:55,830 --> 00:00:58,020
Susan, I understand you're in the toy business.

33
00:00:58,020 --> 00:00:59,030
Yes, I am.

34
00:00:59,030 --> 00:01:00,990
My company manufactures toys and games for children.

35
00:01:00,990 --> 00:01:04,480
Susan's vice-president in charge of new toys and games.

36
00:01:04,480 --> 00:01:06,730
And the marketing of new toys and games.

37
00:01:06,730 --> 00:01:08,910
Can we test a new game for you, Susan?

38
00:01:08,910 --> 00:01:10,460
That's an excellent idea, Michelle.

39
00:01:10,460 --> 00:01:12,360
I happen to have

40
00:01:12,360 --> 00:01:13,190
a game which I brought home to study.

41
00:01:13,190 --> 00:01:13,990
Let us try it!

42
00:01:13,990 --> 00:01:15,560
Do you want to play?

43
00:01:15,560 --> 00:01:19,720
Nicole? Shirley? Audrey?

44
00:01:19,720 --> 00:01:22,940
We tested it last week on twelve- to fifteen-year-olds,

45
00:01:22,940 --> 00:01:25,790
and they found it to be too easy--

46
00:01:25,790 --> 00:01:27,640
in other words ... boring.

47
00:01:27,640 --> 00:01:30,760
We think it might be just right for ten- to twelve-year-olds.

48
00:01:30,760 --> 00:01:31,880
That's us, Susan.

49
00:01:31,880 --> 00:01:35,590
First, you shuffle the deck

50
00:01:35,590 --> 00:01:39,600
and lay them face down.

51
00:01:39,600 --> 00:01:41,870
Then you select the leader.

52
00:01:41,870 --> 00:01:44,210
I'll be the leader.

53
00:01:44,210 --> 00:01:47,150
The leader takes the first ten cards

54
00:01:47,150 --> 00:01:50,310
and lays them face up on this stand.

55
00:01:50,310 --> 00:02:12,530
h-t-e-r-c-z-e-p-e-s.

56
00:02:12,530 --> 00:02:15,220
Everyone gets a turn, going counterclockwise,

57
00:02:15,220 --> 00:02:16,990
left to right.

58
00:02:16,990 --> 00:02:22,950
You have thirty seconds to make a word,

59
00:02:22,950 --> 00:02:25,580
using as many letters as possible.

60
00:02:25,580 --> 00:02:28,230
You get one point for each letter,

61
00:02:28,230 --> 00:02:33,320
plus the person with the longest word gets ten extra points.

62
00:02:33,320 --> 00:02:36,280
The first one to get one hundred points wins.

63
00:02:36,280 --> 00:02:37,600
That's easy.

64
00:02:37,600 --> 00:02:40,280
OK, let's go around the table.

65
00:02:40,280 --> 00:02:49,300
You first, Audrey.

66
00:02:49,300 --> 00:02:56,430
Chest--c-h-e-s-t.

67
00:02:56,430 --> 00:02:57,680
Good.

68
00:02:57,680 --> 00:03:00,060
That's five points.

69
00:03:00,060 --> 00:03:07,330
Next, Nicole.

70
00:03:07,330 --> 00:03:14,630
Three--t-h-r-e-e.

71
00:03:14,630 --> 00:03:15,480
OK.

72
00:03:15,480 --> 00:03:17,640
That's five points also.

73
00:03:17,640 --> 00:03:25,530
It's your turn, Shirley.

74
00:03:25,530 --> 00:03:32,910
Creep--c-r-e-e-p.

75
00:03:32,910 --> 00:03:34,200
Creep.

76
00:03:34,200 --> 00:03:36,100
That's another five-letter word.

77
00:03:36,100 --> 00:03:36,920
Five points.

78
00:03:36,920 --> 00:03:38,850
So far, you're all tied.

79
00:03:38,850 --> 00:03:41,690
Sheet--s-h-e-e-t.

80
00:03:41,690 --> 00:03:45,930
Sheet is a five-letter word.

81
00:03:45,930 --> 00:03:47,410
Michelle, your turn.

82
00:03:47,410 --> 00:03:51,800
Cheese--c-h-e-e-s-e.

83
00:03:51,800 --> 00:03:52,450
Terrific!

84
00:03:52,450 --> 00:03:54,320
Michelle wins with a six-letter word,

85
00:03:54,320 --> 00:03:57,300
plus she gets an additional ten points

86
00:03:57,300 --> 00:03:59,200
for a total of sixteen points.

87
00:03:59,200 --> 00:04:00,990
How are you enjoying the game so far?

88
00:04:00,990 --> 00:04:03,290
I think it's too easy.

89
00:04:03,290 --> 00:04:05,120
Too easy?

90
00:04:05,120 --> 00:04:06,240
Michelle!

91
00:04:06,240 --> 00:04:07,270
It's OK, Harry.

92
00:04:07,270 --> 00:04:08,830
Michelle is quite right.

93
00:04:08,830 --> 00:04:10,900
She just said it's too easy.

94
00:04:10,900 --> 00:04:13,570
Well, I like the game.

95
00:04:13,570 --> 00:04:15,080
I enjoyed lunch, Susan.

96
00:04:15,080 --> 00:04:16,250
Thank you so much,

97
00:04:16,250 --> 00:04:17,580
but we have to get going

98
00:04:17,580 --> 00:04:20,140
to meet the rest of the troop at two o'clock at the museum.

99
00:04:20,140 --> 00:04:22,970
Oh, it was nice meeting all of you.

100
00:04:22,970 --> 00:04:24,550
I hope you have a wonderful time

101
00:04:24,550 --> 00:04:26,380
at the Museum of Natural History.

102
00:04:26,380 --> 00:04:27,400
Good-bye, everybody.

103
00:04:27,400 --> 00:04:28,010
Have a good time.

104
00:04:28,010 --> 00:04:28,960
Bye.

105
00:04:28,960 --> 00:04:29,760
See you in front of the museum at five o'clock.

106
00:04:29,760 --> 00:04:32,150
Oh, OK.

107
00:04:32,150 --> 00:04:32,590
Thanks, Mr. Bennett.

108
00:04:32,590 --> 00:04:33,710
That'll be fine.

109
00:04:33,710 --> 00:04:37,410
And thanks again for the lunch and for the game.

110
00:04:37,410 --> 00:04:39,250
Good-bye, Susan.

111
00:04:39,250 --> 00:04:41,690
It's not a bad game.

112
00:04:41,690 --> 00:04:43,900
It's just ... slow.

113
00:04:43,900 --> 00:04:46,420
Just slow.

114
00:04:46,420 --> 00:04:48,870
You helped save our company a lot of money.

115
00:04:48,870 --> 00:04:59,580
Bye-bye.

116
00:04:59,580 --> 00:05:03,740
You are wonderful with kids.

117
00:05:03,740 --> 00:05:05,810
I am.

118
00:05:05,810 --> 00:05:08,810
Isn't there a conversation that we have to finish?
